Let the device tests collect without numba

Two test-side blockers stop pytest from collecting any numba-cuda-mlir device
test when numba is absent:

  * Compiler.is_available probes `find_spec("numba.cuda")`, which raises
    ModuleNotFoundError with no numba installed - the same defect patched in
    nvmath itself by 0001-disable-numba-cuda-backend.patch. It is evaluated by
    the compiler_param() decorators at module scope, so it takes down collection
    of every parametrized module, mlir params included. Pin it off, matching
    0001; the numba-cuda params then report as unavailable instead of raising.
  * test_cublasdx_numba imports pipeline_extensions from the numba-cuda backend
    at module scope, though it is only used inside two numba-cuda-only tests.
    Defer it to those call sites so the module's mlir params survive.

test_vector_types_numba is deliberately left alone: it parametrizes over numba
`types.*` at module scope, so it cannot be collected without numba at all. Its
mlir params are lost - that module is the one gap in mlir device coverage here.

The perf modules stay uncollectable too, but they are excluded by the -k filter
and carry no mlir params.

Applied by ci/tools/run-nvmath-python-mlir-tests.

